WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.262
Three baselines close the module.

2
00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:05.116
The AD CS that remains may run for years,

3
00:00:05.116 --> 00:00:11.179
so strip every template its workloads don't
need, keep CRLs publishing on schedule,

4
00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:13.229
back up before every change,

5
00:00:13.229 --> 00:00:17.063
and treat CA servers as Tier
0, with keys held in an HSM.

6
00:00:17.063 --> 00:00:21.700
Cloud PKI removes most of that
attack surface but adds its own.

7
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:27.029
There's no built-in PKI administrator
role, so scope admins with custom roles,

8
00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:31.512
keep keys in the TPM, and don't
build production CAs during a trial.

9
00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:36.727
Entra CBA is a relying party, so its
hardening is about trust and binding:

10
00:00:36.727 --> 00:00:42.649
require high-affinity bindings, require
CRL checking, and scope each CA to a group.

11
00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:45.962
Scoping mistakes can lock
users out, so pilot it.

12
00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:47.500
Next, the target.
